10 soldiers with him are saved from a close-in ambush.

766
00:47:45,810 --> 00:47:50,036
In Kandahar Province, Afghanistan, a non-commissioned officer from the female

767
00:47:50,036 --> 00:47:54,262
engagement team, a female engagement team, senses that something isn't

768
00:47:54,262 --> 00:47:58,488
right and directs the infantry platoon away from a 500-pound

769
00:47:58,488 --> 00:48:01,869
IED, saving the lives of a dozen soldiers.

770
00:48:01,870 --> 00:48:06,690
But if you think about it, not only were those soldiers saved

771
00:48:06,690 --> 00:48:09,903
by the decisions of one person, but their

772
00:48:09,903 --> 00:48:15,928
children were saved, and their children's children. Generations were saved by one decision, one person.

773
00:48:15,930 --> 00:48:18,810
But changing the world can happen anywhere, and anyone can do it.

774
00:48:18,810 --> 00:48:21,853
So what starts here can indeed change the world, but

775
00:48:21,853 --> 00:48:25,809
the question is, what will the world look like after you change it?

776
00:48:25,810 --> 00:48:28,242
Well, I'm confident that it will look much, much better,

777
00:48:28,242 --> 00:48:30,674
but if you'll humor this old sailor for just a

778
00:48:30,674 --> 00:48:34,809
moment, I have a few suggestions that might help you on your way to a better world.

779
00:48:34,810 --> 00:48:38,238
And while these lessons were learned during my time in the military,

780
00:48:38,238 --> 00:48:42,809
I can assure you that it matters not whether you ever served a day in uniform.

781
00:48:42,810 --> 00:48:48,030
It matters not your gender, your ethnic or religious background, your origin, or your nationality.

782
00:48:48,030 --> 00:48:52,030
It matters not your background, your orientation, or your social status.

783
00:48:52,030 --> 00:48:55,578
Our struggles in this world are similar, and the lessons

784
00:48:55,578 --> 00:48:59,126
to overcome those struggles and to move forward, changing ourselves

785
00:48:59,126 --> 00:49:03,029
and changing the world around us, will apply equally to all.

786
00:49:03,030 --> 00:49:05,116
I've been a Navy SEAL for 36

787
00:49:05,116 --> 00:49:07,550
years, but it all began when I

788
00:49:07,550 --> 00:49:10,680
left UT for basic SEAL training in Coronado, California.

789
00:49:11,030 --> 00:49:13,160
Basic SEAL training is six months of

790
00:49:13,160 --> 00:49:18,029
long, torturous runs in the soft sand, midnight swims in the cold water off San Diego.

791
00:49:18,030 --> 00:49:23,030
Half-school courses, unending calisthenics, days without sleep, and always being cold, wet, and miserable.

792
00:49:23,030 --> 00:49:27,868
It is six months of being constantly harassed by professionally

793
00:49:27,868 --> 00:49:32,706
trained warriors who seek to find the weak of mind

794
00:49:32,706 --> 00:49:38,028
and body and eliminate them from ever becoming a Navy SEAL.

795
00:49:38,030 --> 00:49:41,302
But the training also seeks to find those

796
00:49:41,302 --> 00:49:47,029
students who can lead in an environment of constant stress, chaos, failure, and hardships.

797
00:49:48,030 --> 00:49:53,030
To me, basic SEAL training was a lifetime of challenges crammed into six months.

798
00:49:53,030 --> 00:49:55,722
So here are the ten lessons I learned from basic

799
00:49:55,722 --> 00:49:57,875
SEAL training that hopefully will be of value

800
00:49:57,875 --> 00:50:00,028
to you as you move forward in life.

801
00:50:00,030 --> 00:50:02,780
Every morning in SEAL training, my instructors, who

802
00:50:02,780 --> 00:50:05,186
at the time were all Vietnam veterans,

803
00:50:05,186 --> 00:50:07,592
would show up in my barracks room,

804
00:50:07,592 --> 00:50:11,029
and the first thing they'd do was inspect my bed.

805
00:50:11,030 --> 00:50:14,172
If you did it right, the corners would be square,

806
00:50:14,172 --> 00:50:16,686
the covers would be pulled tight, the pillows

807
00:50:16,686 --> 00:50:22,028
centered just under the headboard. And the extra blanket folded neatly at the foot of the rack.

808
00:50:22,030 --> 00:50:30,030
It was a simple task, mundane at best, but every morning we were required to make our bed to perfection.

809
00:50:30,030 --> 00:50:32,590
It seemed a little ridiculous at the time,

810
00:50:32,590 --> 00:50:35,150
particularly in light of the fact that we

811
00:50:35,150 --> 00:50:38,030
were aspiring to be real warriors, tough, battle-hardened SEALs.

812
00:50:38,030 --> 00:50:45,030
But the wisdom of this simple act has been proven to me many times over.

813
00:50:45,030 --> 00:50:47,030
If you make your bed every morning, you're not going to be able to sleep.

814
00:50:47,030 --> 00:50:50,030
You will have accomplished the first task of the day.

815
00:50:50,030 --> 00:50:52,575
It will give you a small sense of

816
00:50:52,575 --> 00:50:54,484
pride, and it will encourage you

817
00:50:54,484 --> 00:50:57,029
to do another task, and another, and another.

818
00:50:57,030 --> 00:51:02,030
And by the end of the day, that one task completed will have turned into many tasks completed.

819
00:51:02,030 --> 00:51:07,030
Making your bed will also reinforce the fact that the little things in life matter.

820
00:51:07,030 --> 00:51:12,030
If you can't do the little things right, you'll never be able to do the big things right.

821
00:51:12,030 --> 00:51:13,848
And if by chance you have a miserable day, you

822
00:51:13,848 --> 00:51:16,029
will come home to a bed that is more important to you.

823
00:51:16,030 --> 00:51:21,310
You will come home to a bed that is made, that you made.

824
00:51:21,310 --> 00:51:25,310
And a made bed gives you encouragement that tomorrow will be better.

825
00:51:25,310 --> 00:51:29,310
So if you want to change the world, start off by making your bed.

826
00:51:29,310 --> 00:51:37,040
During SEAL training, the students are all broken down into boat crews.

827
00:51:37,040 --> 00:51:39,267
Each crew is seven students, three on

828
00:51:39,267 --> 00:51:41,494
each side of a small rubber boat,

829
00:51:41,494 --> 00:51:44,039
and one coxswain to help guide the dinghy.

830
00:51:44,040 --> 00:51:45,424
Every day, your boat crew forms

831
00:51:45,424 --> 00:51:47,500
up on the beach and is instructed to get

832
00:51:47,500 --> 00:51:50,038
through the surf zone and paddle several miles down the coast.

833
00:51:50,040 --> 00:51:53,477
In the winter, the surf off San Diego can get

834
00:51:53,477 --> 00:51:56,227
to be eight to ten feet high, and

835
00:51:56,227 --> 00:52:01,039
it is exceedingly difficult to paddle through the plunging surf unless everyone digs in.

836
00:52:01,040 --> 00:52:06,040
Every paddle must be synchronized to the stroke count of the coxswain.

837
00:52:06,040 --> 00:52:08,373
Everyone must exert equal effort, or the

838
00:52:08,373 --> 00:52:13,039
boat will turn against the wave and be unceremoniously dumped back on the beach.

839
00:52:13,040 --> 00:52:17,040
For the boat to make it to its destination, everyone must paddle.

840
00:52:17,040 --> 00:52:20,040
You can't change the world alone.

841
00:52:20,040 --> 00:52:22,040
You will need some help.

842
00:52:22,040 --> 00:52:25,640
And to truly get from your starting point to your

843
00:52:25,640 --> 00:52:27,800
destination takes friends, colleagues, the goodwill

844
00:52:27,800 --> 00:52:31,040
of strangers, and a strong coxswain to guide you.

845
00:52:31,040 --> 00:52:35,040
If you want to change the world, find someone to help you paddle.

846
00:52:35,040 --> 00:52:44,320
Over a few weeks of difficult training, my SEAL class, which started with 150 men, was down to just 42.

847
00:52:44,320 --> 00:52:47,320
There are now six boat crews of seven men each.

848
00:52:47,320 --> 00:52:49,492
I was in the boat with the

849
00:52:49,492 --> 00:52:51,974
tall guys, but the best boat crew we

850
00:52:51,974 --> 00:52:56,318
had was made up of the little guys, the munchkin crew, we called them.

851
00:52:56,320 --> 00:52:59,320
No one was over five foot five.

852
00:52:59,320 --> 00:53:01,912
The munchkin boat crew had one American

853
00:53:01,912 --> 00:53:04,504
Indian, one African American, one Polish American,

854
00:53:04,504 --> 00:53:06,355
one Greek American, one Italian

855
00:53:06,355 --> 00:53:09,317
American, and two tough kids from the Midwest.

856
00:53:09,320 --> 00:53:14,320
They out paddled, out ran, and out swam all the other boat crews.

857
00:53:14,320 --> 00:53:17,320
The big men in the other boat crews would always make great progress.

858
00:53:17,320 --> 00:53:20,748
The good natured fun of the tiny little

859
00:53:20,748 --> 00:53:24,176
flippers the munchkins put on their tiny little

860
00:53:24,176 --> 00:53:26,318
feet prior to every swim.

861
00:53:26,320 --> 00:53:29,653
But somehow these little guys from every corner of the

862
00:53:29,653 --> 00:53:32,986
nation and the world always had the last laugh, swimming

863
00:53:32,986 --> 00:53:35,652
faster than everyone and reaching the shore long

864
00:53:35,652 --> 00:53:37,318
before the rest of us.

865
00:53:37,320 --> 00:53:39,320
SEAL training was a great equalizer.

866
00:53:39,320 --> 00:53:41,605
Nothing mattered but your will to

867
00:53:41,605 --> 00:53:43,890
succeed, not your color, not your

868
00:53:43,890 --> 00:53:46,175
ethnic background, not your education, not

869
00:53:46,175 --> 00:53:47,317
your social status.

870
00:53:47,320 --> 00:53:51,493
If you want to change the world, measure a person by the

871
00:53:51,493 --> 00:53:55,319
size of their heart, not by the size of their flippers.

872
00:53:55,320 --> 00:54:03,320
Several times a week, the instructors would line up the class and do a uniform inspection. It was exceptionally thorough.

873
00:54:03,320 --> 00:54:11,320
Your hat had to be perfectly starched, your uniform immaculately pressed, your belt buckle shiny and void of any smudges.

874
00:54:11,320 --> 00:54:14,630
But it seemed that no matter how much effort you put into

875
00:54:14,630 --> 00:54:17,388
starching your hat or pressing your uniform or polishing your

876
00:54:17,388 --> 00:54:19,319
belt buckle, it just wasn't good enough.

877
00:54:19,320 --> 00:54:21,320
The instructors would find something wrong.

878
00:54:21,320 --> 00:54:25,536
For failing the uniform inspection, the student had to run, fully clothed,

879
00:54:25,536 --> 00:54:29,049
into the surf zone, then wet from head to toe,

880
00:54:29,049 --> 00:54:31,157
roll around on the beach until

881
00:54:31,157 --> 00:54:34,319
every part of your body was covered with sand.

882
00:54:34,320 --> 00:54:37,716
The effect was known as a sugar cookie.

883
00:54:37,716 --> 00:54:43,659
You stayed in the uniform the rest of the day, cold, wet, and sandy.

884
00:54:43,660 --> 00:54:46,387
There were many a student who just couldn't accept the

885
00:54:46,387 --> 00:54:49,114
fact that all their efforts were in vain, that no

886
00:54:49,114 --> 00:54:52,659
matter how hard they tried to get the uniform right, it went unappreciated.

887
00:54:52,660 --> 00:54:54,660
Those students didn't make it through training.

888
00:54:54,660 --> 00:54:58,660
Those students didn't understand the purpose of the drill.

889
00:54:58,660 --> 00:55:02,660
You were never going to succeed. You were never going to have a perfect uniform.

890
00:55:02,660 --> 00:55:05,660
The instructors weren't going to allow it.

891
00:55:05,660 --> 00:55:09,660
Sometimes, no matter how well you prepare or how well you perform,

892
00:55:09,660 --> 00:55:15,660
you still end up as a sugar cookie. It's just the way life is sometimes.

893
00:55:15,660 --> 00:55:21,660
If you want to change the world, get over being a sugar cookie and keep moving forward.

894
00:55:21,660 --> 00:55:24,736
Every day during training, you were challenged with

895
00:55:24,736 --> 00:55:27,812
multiple physical events, long runs, long swims, obstacle

896
00:55:27,812 --> 00:55:31,658
courses, hours of calisthenics, something designed to test your mettle.

897
00:55:31,660 --> 00:55:34,660
Every event had standards, times you had to meet.

898
00:55:34,660 --> 00:55:37,066
If you failed to meet those times,

899
00:55:37,066 --> 00:55:39,472
those standards, your name was posted on

900
00:55:39,472 --> 00:55:45,659
a list, and at the end of the day, those on the list were invited to a circus.

901
00:55:45,660 --> 00:55:47,296
A circus was two hours of

902
00:55:47,296 --> 00:55:48,932
additional calisthenics, designed to wear you

903
00:55:48,932 --> 00:55:51,659
down, to break your spirit, to force you to quit.

904
00:55:51,660 --> 00:55:54,660
No one wanted a circus.

905
00:55:54,660 --> 00:55:57,660
A circus meant that for that day, you didn't measure up.

906
00:55:57,660 --> 00:55:58,932
A circus meant more

907
00:55:58,932 --> 00:56:00,841
fatigue, and more fatigue meant that

908
00:56:00,841 --> 00:56:02,750
the following day would be more

909
00:56:02,750 --> 00:56:04,659
difficult, and more circuses were likely.

910
00:56:04,660 --> 00:56:11,660
But at some time during SEAL training, everyone, everyone made the circus list.

911
00:56:11,660 --> 00:56:17,660
But an interesting thing happened to those who were constantly struggling. To those who were constantly on the list.

912
00:56:17,660 --> 00:56:24,660
Over time, those students who did two hours of extra calisthenics got stronger and stronger.

913
00:56:24,660 --> 00:56:28,660
The pain of the circuses built inner strength and physical resiliency.

914
00:56:28,660 --> 00:56:31,660
Life is filled with circuses.

915
00:56:31,660 --> 00:56:33,660
You will fail.

916
00:56:33,660 --> 00:56:35,660
You will likely fail often.

917
00:56:35,660 --> 00:56:36,660
It will be painful.

918
00:56:36,660 --> 00:56:38,660
It will be discouraging.

919
00:56:38,660 --> 00:56:41,660
At times, it will test you to your very core.

920
00:56:41,660 --> 00:56:46,660
But if you don't, if you want to change the world, don't be afraid of the circuses.

921
00:56:46,660 --> 00:56:51,660
At least twice a week, the trainees were required to run the obstacle course.

922
00:56:51,660 --> 00:56:53,887
The obstacle course contained 25 obstacles, including a

923
00:56:53,887 --> 00:56:55,796
10-foot wall, a 30-foot cargo net,

924
00:56:55,796 --> 00:56:58,341
a barbed wire crawl, to name a few.

925
00:56:58,660 --> 00:57:02,660
But the most challenging obstacle was the slide for life.

926
00:57:02,660 --> 00:57:07,660
It had a three-level, 30-foot tower at one end, and a one-level tower at the other.

927
00:57:07,660 --> 00:57:10,660
In between was a 200-foot long rope.

928
00:57:10,660 --> 00:57:12,993
You had to climb the three-tiered tower,

929
00:57:12,993 --> 00:57:15,326
and once at the top, you grabbed

930
00:57:15,326 --> 00:57:17,326
the rope, swung underneath the rope,

931
00:57:17,326 --> 00:57:21,659
and pulled yourself hand over hand until you got to the other end.

932
00:57:21,660 --> 00:57:26,660
The record for the obstacle course had stood for years when my class began in 1977.

933
00:57:26,660 --> 00:57:28,660
The record seemed unbeatable

934
00:57:28,660 --> 00:57:34,660
until one day a student decided to go down the slide for life head first.

935
00:57:34,660 --> 00:57:38,660
Instead of swinging his body underneath the rope and inching his way down,

936
00:57:38,660 --> 00:57:42,660
he bravely mounted the top of the rope and thrust himself forward.

937
00:57:42,660 --> 00:57:47,660
It was a dangerous move, seemingly foolish and fraught with risk.

938
00:57:47,660 --> 00:57:49,660
Failure could mean injury and being dropped from the course.

939
00:57:49,660 --> 00:57:53,660
Without hesitation, the student slid down the rope perilously fast.

940
00:57:53,660 --> 00:57:57,660
Instead of several minutes, it only took him half that time.

941
00:57:57,660 --> 00:58:01,660
And by the end of the course, he had broken the record.

942
00:58:01,660 --> 00:58:03,660
If you want to change the world,

943
00:58:03,660 --> 00:58:08,910
sometimes you have to slide down the obstacles head first.

944
00:58:08,910 --> 00:58:11,243
During the land warfare phase of training, the

945
00:58:11,243 --> 00:58:13,284
students are flown out to San Clemente

946
00:58:13,284 --> 00:58:15,909
Island, which lies off the coast of San Diego.

947
00:58:15,910 --> 00:58:19,910
The waters off San Clemente are a breeding ground for the great white sharks.

948
00:58:19,910 --> 00:58:23,910
To pass SEAL training, there are a series of long swims that must be completed.

949
00:58:23,910 --> 00:58:25,910
One is the night swim.

950
00:58:25,910 --> 00:58:28,364
Before the swim, the instructors joyfully

951
00:58:28,364 --> 00:58:30,818
brief the students on all the

952
00:58:30,818 --> 00:58:34,908
species of sharks that inhabit the waters off San Clemente.

953
